    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "Three constructions are supported. (1) Hyphenated status reports like F-dim/F-bright and H-silent/H-loud show a stable two-slot frame: a subsystem target prefix plus a state/quality predicate. (2) Localized region terms like R-edges/T-edges and R-corners/Bk-corners show a stable face selector plus region suffix. (3) Xa/Xb form a minimal pair with stable X='action failed' plus a contrasting suspect-part slot. Other items are left lexical because no compositional multi-entry paradigm is securely supported.",
